olivia: Heads-up — I opened a small PR to harmonize the streaming + pagination examples across py/ts/go. The main issues: cursor name changed from `cursor_id` -> `page_cursor`, and the streaming snippet needs a retry wrapper in all three languages. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4128 :eyes:

kevin: looking now. Quick q — do we standardize on an async iterator example for Python or show both sync + async?

olivia: prefer async iterator for streaming in Python (most real apps use async). Keep a tiny sync example for backwards-compat in a separate one-liner comment.

maya: found a small bug in the Go example — we were calling NextPage() before checking for EOF. I'll paste a patch: ```go // before
for {
  page, err := client.FetchPage(ctx, req)
  // process page
  req.PageCursor = page.NextCursor
}
// after
for {
  page, err := client.FetchPage(ctx, req)
  if err == io.EOF { break }
  if err != nil { return err }
  // process page
  req.PageCursor = page.NextCursor
}
```

kevin: nice catch. Also changed the field name in the TS snippet to `pageCursor`, updated types. For retries I wrapped the streaming read with our helper `withExponentialRetries()` — shows jitter/backoff behavior. Example: ```ts const stream = await withExponentialRetries(() => sdk.openStream(req), { retries: 3 }) for await (const chunk of stream) { console.log(chunk) } ```

ryan: heads-up — CI flagged a flaky test around pagination cursor serialization in the examples test harness. I re-ran and it failed once (timeout on the mock stream). Suggest we add a short test that simulates a reconnect and asserts the cursor is preserved. I can add that if folks agree.

olivia: yes please add the reconnect test, @ryan. Keep it minimal (spawn mock server -> send two partial streams -> reconnect -> assert pageCursor persisted).

maya: will update the Go example tests too. Also note: we should add a short note in the docs about why `page_cursor` was renamed to `pageCursor` in TS and `page_cursor` in the API response — tiny section explaining camelCase vs snake_case mapping for SDKs.

kevin: added that note in the PR description. Also pinned the code sample versions (py: 1.4.0, ts: 2.3.1, go: 0.9.0) to avoid future mismatch.

docs-bot: CI / examples-check — build passed for docs site (examples lint) on commit 7a9f2c. Tests: 1 failed (pagination-reconnect-test) — rerun triggered. :information_desk_person:

ryan: rerun passed. I'll push the small test to the PR branch and link it here in a minute.

olivia: awesome — plan for landing: kevin + maya to squash small fixes, ryan to add the reconnect test, then I'll merge after one more quick review. Targeting EOD PST. :thumbsup:

kevin: assigned myself to squash and tidy commit messages.

maya: assigned to update Go and docs note, will do in next 30m.

olivia: thanks everyone — ping if you hit anything blocking.
